# console write faults and the panel goes black.  Same fix uke and asteroids
# carry in their 27 series (zzzzz-video-console-physical-fb.patch); 0543 covers
# the PE_create_console() call, this one covers every initialize_screen() call.
0552-k60-video-console-physical-fb.patch
# 0553 painted a magenta band just before vc_initialize(), which clears the screen
# microseconds later -- the band could never be seen, so it proved nothing.  This
# one paints at the END of initialize_screen(), after that clear, so it survives:
# magenta with no text means the kernel reached this point with the console still
# off, text means the console works, black means the kernel never got here.
0554-k60-fb-witness-tail.patch
# 0556: fill the whole framebuffer with the kernel's own v_rowbytes/v_height.
# The 0554 eight-row band showed magenta across the panel instead of at the
# top, so either initialize_screen() runs with several v_offset values or the
# stride disagrees.  A uniform fill means the geometry is right; remaining
# bands mean the stride is wrong and their pitch measures the ratio.
0556-k60-fb-full-witness.patch
